The '''Balboa football league system''' is a series of interconnected leagues for [[association football]] clubs in [[Balboa]], organised by the [[Federació Balboana de Futbol]] (FBF). The system operates on a promotion and relegation basis, with the '''La Lliga de l'Istme''' (commonly known as '''La Lliga''') at the top, followed by the '''Lliga de Futbol Balboa 2''' (LFB2), '''Lliga de Futbol Balboa 3''' (LFB3), and '''Lliga de Futbol Balboa 4''' (LFB4). Below the national tiers, a series of regional leagues — organised by the provincial football associations — form the base of the pyramid.

The system is characterised by its Abyalan split-season format, in which each year is divided into two short tournaments — the '''Apertura''' (opening) and the '''Clausura''' (closing) — each producing its own champion. The two tournament champions then contest the '''Gran Final''' to determine the year's overall champion. The format, which is shared with most Abyalan leagues, produces two tournament titles and one overall title per year.

== Structure ==

The Balboa football league system comprises four national tiers and a series of regional leagues below them. Promotion and relegation operates between all four national tiers and between the fourth tier and the regional leagues.

