=== La Lliga de l'Istme (Tier 1) ===

{{main|La Lliga de l'Istme}}

La Lliga de l'Istme is the top tier of Balboan football. It comprises 16 clubs and operates on the Abyalan split-season format. The bottom two clubs are automatically relegated to LFB2; the 15th-placed club enters a promotion-relegation playoff against the third-placed club in LFB2.

=== Lliga de Futbol Balboa 2 (Tier 2) ===

{{main|Lliga de Futbol Balboa 2}}

LFB2 is the second tier of Balboan football. It comprises 18 clubs in a single group. The top two clubs are automatically promoted to La Lliga; the third-placed club enters the promotion-relegation playoff. The bottom two clubs are automatically relegated to LFB3; the 16th-placed club enters a promotion-relegation playoff.

=== Lliga de Futbol Balboa 3 (Tier 3) ===

{{main|Lliga de Futbol Balboa 3}}

LFB3 is the third tier of Balboan football. It comprises 20 clubs divided into two regional groups: the '''Grup Jala–Nurra–Tramuntana''' (10 clubs from the interior and northern provinces) and the '''Grup Estret–Migjorn''' (10 clubs from the corridor and southern provinces). The winners of each group are automatically promoted to LFB2; the runners-up enter the promotion-relegation playoff. The bottom club in each group is automatically relegated to LFB4; the 9th-placed club in each group enters a promotion-relegation playoff.

=== Lliga de Futbol Balboa 4 (Tier 4) ===

{{main|Lliga de Futbol Balboa 4}}

LFB4 is the fourth and lowest national tier of Balboan football. It comprises 24 clubs divided into four regional groups of six clubs each. The winners of each group are automatically promoted to LFB3; the runners-up enter the promotion-relegation playoffs. The bottom club in each group is automatically relegated to its respective regional league; the 5th-placed club in each group enters a promotion-relegation playoff.

== Season format ==

All four national tiers operate on the Abyalan split-season format. The year is divided into two short tournaments:

* The '''Apertura''' (opening tournament), played from February to June
* The '''Clausura''' (closing tournament), played from August to December

In each tournament, the clubs play a single round-robin within their group (La Lliga: 15 matches; LFB2: 17 matches; LFB3: 9 matches per group; LFB4: 5 matches per group). The top finishers in each tournament then enter a short playoff — the '''liguilla''' — to determine the tournament champion. The Apertura and Clausura champions then contest the '''Gran Final''' to determine the year's overall champion.

In La Lliga, the liguilla comprises the top eight clubs after the round-robin, who play a single-elimination bracket (quarter-finals, semi-finals, final). The winner is the tournament champion. The Gran Final is a single match at a neutral venue; if the same club wins both the Apertura and the Clausura, the Gran Final is not contested and the club is crowned overall champion automatically.

Relegation is determined by the aggregate table — the combined results of both the Apertura and Clausura round-robins — rather than by the results of either tournament individually. This prevents a club from avoiding relegation by performing well in one tournament while collapsing in the other.

== Promotion and relegation ==

Promotion and relegation between the tiers operates as follows:

=== La Lliga ↔ LFB2 ===

* '''Automatic relegation''': Bottom 2 clubs in the La Lliga aggregate table
* '''Playoff''': 15th-placed La Lliga club vs. 3rd-placed LFB2 club (two legs)
* '''Automatic promotion''': Top 2 clubs in the LFB2 aggregate table

=== LFB2 ↔ LFB3 ===

* '''Automatic relegation''': Bottom 2 clubs in the LFB2 aggregate table
* '''Playoff''': 16th-placed LFB2 club vs. 2nd-placed LFB3 club from the opposite group (two legs)
* '''Automatic promotion''': Winners of each LFB3 group
* '''Playoff promotion''': Runners-up in each LFB3 group enter the playoff

=== LFB3 ↔ LFB4 ===

* '''Automatic relegation''': Bottom club in each LFB3 group
* '''Playoff''': 9th-placed club in each LFB3 group vs. best LFB4 runner-up (two legs)
* '''Automatic promotion''': Winners of each LFB4 group
* '''Playoff promotion''': Runners-up in each LFB4 group enter the playoff

=== LFB4 ↔ Regional leagues ===

* '''Automatic relegation''': Bottom club in each LFB4 group
* '''Playoff''': 5th-placed club in each LFB4 group vs. best regional league runner-up (two legs)
* '''Automatic promotion''': Winners of each regional league (subject to licensing)
* '''Playoff promotion''': Runners-up in each regional league enter the playoff

